# With no .reqntid %tid.x lies below 1024 on any block (PTX ISA §10.1,
# §10.2), so `shl.b32` of %tid.x by 28 leaves 32 bits and keeps its low
# four: the store's thread test reads %tid.x mod 16 == 0 (ptxas 13.4:
# `SHF.R.U32.HI R0, RZ, 0x1c, R0`, `ISETP.NE.U32`, `@P0 EXIT`).
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/tid_range.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd1], %r1; // [<block 1>] (%tid.x mod 16) == 0 | exec <= 1/thread | global store [param_0] sectors/req ? (block shape unknown: no .reqntid; pass --launch){{$}}
